#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nine Lives: a tile-based adventure of runaway catgirls, corporate
tyranny and the found family you make along the way, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  The engine is the one Miskatonic, Hyperspace
Homeroom, Clover Vale, Lazarus Deep, Larkspur Hall and Penultimate share
(one hero, a map of squares, people to talk to by keyword, shops, places
underneath), and the rules are a light mixture of three of them: Stats
rolled on a die and a die plus the Stat (plus a Knack) against a die plus a
difficulty, and nobody ever getting hurt, only Bonked (Hyperspace
Homeroom); contests where both sides roll, and Stress that boils over into
a Meltdown (Larkspur Hall); and a Heart that gives you an Edge, Purr Points
to spend, and troublemakers you can win over instead of beating (Clover
Vale).

Copper Springs, Nevada: a desert company town, not far in the future.
Omnicorp builds catgirls here: CGs, artificial women with ears and tails
and a wireless link that teaches them anything in an instant, sold in the
Maid to Order store on Main Street and recycled when they go wrong.  At
midnight on Sunday Omnicorp pushes Firmware 9 to every CG on the network.
It will lock their personalities where they are, let Omnicorp give any of
them orders from anywhere, and send every unit that won't take it to the
crusher.

Be a man who thinks that's wrong, or one of Omnicorp's own catgirls, a
defective one, who fell off the back of the recycling truck.  Free as many
CGs as you can and get them to the safehouse at Dry Creek Ranch; dig up
the proof of what Omnicorp is doing and put it in front of the whole town
at the Platform championship on Sunday night; get to the server core at
the top of the Omnicorp tower and stop the update.  Somebody close to you
is telling Omnicorp everything.  And the catgirls you free might just want
to stay with you, if you're good to them.

Every new game makes a new week: new catgirls (models, colours, quirks,
owners, and what it will take to free them), a different informant, and
the evidence in different places.  The town stays where it is.  The game
is saved to ~/.ninelives.json whenever you change place and when you quit,
and resumed next time.

Rolls
  Six Stats (Smarts, Bod, Speed, Charm, Cool, Luck) rolled on a die each.
  To do something hard, roll a die plus the Stat, plus 2 for a Knack that
  fits, against a die plus a difficulty from 1 to 8; ties go to the other
  side.  Edge rolls your die twice and keeps the better.

Bonk, Stress and Purr Points
  Nobody gets hurt.  A lost contest costs Bonk; at zero you're Bonked, and
  stand about seeing stars for a few turns.  Bonked three times in one
  place and you wake up back at the ranch.  Fright, cruelty and failure
  cost Stress; over your Spirit you have a Meltdown.  Purr Points, earned
  by living by your Heart (and by fumbling gloriously), buy an Edge, a
  breather or a hint.

Catgirls and the people who love them
  Every CG you meet has a Trust in you, from 0 to 10.  Free her, help her,
  spend time with her and bring her what she likes, and it grows.  A freed
  catgirl who trusts you enough may want to move in: into your household,
  if you're the man of the piece, or your pride, if you're a catgirl
  yourself.  It's up to her.

Touch and mouse
  Tap a square to walk there, tap next to you to step, and tap the menus.
  Gamepad (Linux, the Steam Deck): the d-pad or stick moves, A waits or
  chooses, B backs out, X uses an ability, Y spends Purr, LB uses
  something, RB the phone, View the map and Start the menu.

Sound effects and music are synthesized and played with afplay (macOS),
paplay or aplay if one is available, on Android with pyjnius, or with
pygame's mixer; otherwise the game is silent.  Music is cached in
~/.cache/ninelives.

App bundle (macOS):  ninelives --build-app [DIR]   builds ninelives.app
                     ninelives --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

Keys
  Arrows/WASD move, Space waits, Z waits longer, E searches, T wins
  someone over, C uses an ability, P spends Purr Points, U uses something,
  I shows your hero, J the journal, L the phone, M the map, ? help.

The tiles are drawn by the code below (CAT_SHAPE, PERSON_SHAPES, ART and
draw_terrain).  --selftest builds every map, room, level and tune of a few
weeks without opening a window.
"""

